{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/acciento89-bot/sammlerraum/pulls/1","id":4584313881,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUfIdT88AAAABET8UGQ","html_url":"https://github.com/acciento89-bot/sammlerraum/pull/1","diff_url":"https://github.com/acciento89-bot/sammlerraum/pull/1.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/acciento89-bot/sammlerraum/pull/1.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/acciento89-bot/sammlerraum/issues/1","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/acciento89-bot/sammlerraum/pulls/1/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/acciento89-bot/sammlerraum/pulls/1/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/acciento89-bot/sammlerraum/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/acciento89-bot/sammlerraum/issues/1/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/acciento89-bot/sammlerraum/statuses/9b81b9f4ba21d7a4c2855ef8b592bf7a2beb25a8","number":1,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Sammlerraum V1: private collector workflows and verified data transfers","user":{"login":"acciento89-bot","id":309368001,"node_id":"U_kgDOEnCUwQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/309368001?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/acciento89-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/acciento89-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acciento89-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acciento89-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acciento89-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acciento89-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acciento89-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acciento89-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acciento89-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acciento89-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acciento89-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Sammlerraum V1 implementation draft. Phase08 provides private import/export, insurance and PDF workflows. Phase09 Tasks1–5 now implement database-backed roles, atomic ownership transfer, recipient-bound invitations, granular read-only sharing and actual same-transaction audit integration.\n\nTransfers preserve original financial provenance and private associated data. Shares remain separate from membership, exclude private fields by default, hash bearer tokens, enforce PIN attempt budgets and reauthorize actual image/PDF bytes before and after storage I/O. The responsive DE/EN viewer supports selected details and bounded exports.\n\nActual core mutation producers now record original actor/source and strict before/after facts for items, collections/nodes, condition/category, grading, manual valuations, personal locations, tags and typed fields, media/documents, lifecycle/catalogue changes, money authoring/classification/revocation, imports, roles and invitation/share management. Unknown legacy units stay unknown; exact financial digits and provenance are preserved. A separate erasable subject-user FK supports role history without embedding account identity in immutable JSON. Narrow receipt-bound Viewer acceptance/self-removal does not authorize general edits. No audit-write HTTP route; tokens, receipt/evidence text, invitation emails, storage keys and private note bodies are excluded.\n\nVerified source 3e156ec / evidence 9b81b9f: closing 1,415 passing tests in 116 files, zero skips, covering the entire domain with native PostgreSQL enabled plus all non-domain native CI selections. The regular suite separately passes 1,542 tests with 936 explicitly native-disabled cases; these selections overlap. Root/web strict types, lint and full production build pass. Seven compiled DE/EN desktop/mobile real-cookie browser journeys pass. Eleven frozen forward migration receipts are unchanged and both retained guarded test databases have empty schema diffs. A previous CI certificate-race fixture was corrected to a native late writer after app writers gained the earlier actor fence; genuine uniqueness/rollback assertions remain. Latest CI success is not yet claimed.\n\nNext: Task6 conflict-aware restoration, followed by Task7 collaboration management UI and one independent whole-phase review. Reviewed total remains 48/91; five Phase09 implementations are locally verified and pending that review. This remains an open draft: no application merge/deployment, live provider/mail/customer operation, other apps/stores or automation.","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-20T13:54:16Z","updated_at":"2026-11-07T08:14:58Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"acciento89-bot:work/sammlerraum-v1","ref":"work/sammlerraum-v1","repo":{"id":1374821711,"node_id":"R_kgDOUfIdTw","name":"sammlerraum","full_name":"acciento89-bot/sammlerraum","owner":{"login":"acciento89-bot","id":309368001,"node_id":"U_kgDOEnCUwQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/309368001?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/acciento89-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/acciento89-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acciento89-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acciento89-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acciento89-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acciento89-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acciento89-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acciento89-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acciento89-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acciento89-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/acciento89-bot/re